d 'TVTOOLS': module to build and analyze time-varying exposure data for survival analysis
d
d  tvtools is a suite of commands that turns prescription,
d treatment, and other episode records into analysis-ready
d time-varying survival data. tvexpose converts episode records
d into person-time intervals with categorical, ever/current/former,
d cumulative-duration, recency, and cumulative-dose exposure
d definitions, including grace periods, lags, and washout windows;
d tvmerge combines several time-varying exposure datasets into one
d interval set; tvevent attaches single, competing, or recurring
d events and supports gap-time clocks; tvage, tvband, and tvsplit
d split follow-up on age, calendar, elapsed-time, and multiple
d Lexis timescales; and tvpanel builds entry-anchored person-period
d panels. tvbuild, with the specification frame written by tvspec,
d performs the whole construction as one validated, transactional
d call and records a provenance manifest. tvdiagnose reports
d coverage, gaps, overlaps, and exposure summaries, and tvweight
d estimates inverse probability of treatment weights (optionally
d stabilized), overlap and matching weights, and inverse
d probability of censoring weights for marginal structural models.
d Dialogs are provided for tvexpose, tvmerge, and tvevent, and the
d tvtools command lists the suite. Results are returned in r(). 
d
d KW: time-varying exposure
d KW: survival analysis
d KW: stset
d KW: person-time
d KW: episode data
d KW: prescription data
d KW: pharmacoepidemiology
d KW: Lexis expansion
d KW: competing risks
d KW: inverse probability weighting
d KW: IPTW
d KW: IPCW
d KW: marginal structural models
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author: Timothy P Copeland, Karolinska Institutet
d Support: email timothy.copeland@@ki.se
d
